Subject: leak on pipeline near {ADDRESS}

We had a pipeline rupture near {ADDRESS} at 22:57 on May 18. The volume released was metered at 955,000 m³. The leak appears to be through the pipe body or a weld. Product got onto the pipeline right of way and also onto neighbouring land. After the rupture, the segment couldn't hold pressure. We also had a fire at our facility at the same time. I'm still gathering info but wanted to get this to you ASAP. The fire was on our equipment. I'll be on site tomorrow to assess the situation.

{NAME}, Area Supervisor

Subject: leak on 16" main near {ADDRESS}

Just got the SCADA alarm at 15:50 today-16" main zero pressure, metered loss 988 m³. Local crew rolled out, found the rupture on the body of the pipe, looks like a weld fail. Product hit the ROW and went a bit onto the neighbour's field. Line let go completely, couldn't hold any pressure. Still isolating upstream/downstream, but the hole's confirmed open. That's what we got.

{NAME}, Field Op

